<title>GERMANY: German cocoa imports up at 303,975 T in 1996.</title>
<headline>German cocoa imports up at 303,975 T in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cocoa bean imports in 1996 totalled 303,975 tonnes compared with 285,097 tonnes in 1995, official data showed.</p>
<p>The total included imports from countries outside and within the European Union.</p>
<p>Imports from the EU in 1996 totalled 121.8 tonnes compared with 105.8 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>Imports in December were 17,965 tonnes, down from 30,486 in November and 26,420 tonnes in December 1995.</p>
<p>December import value of 39.36 million marks compared with 55.26 million the year before.</p>
<p>Leading suppliers in the 12 months were Ivory Coast with 180,494 tonnes, Ghana with 53,277, Indonesia 26,329 and Nigeria with 14,053, excluding beans for toll grinding.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
